      "biography": {
        "value": "<h2>Description</h2><p>This large plant monster looks like a dead but still standing tree until it begins to move, a wicked face opening up on its side as it uses its roots to walk towards its victims, its branches flailing for their heads like grasping limbs. Sometimes also known as a “crawler,” but it's not a worm at all…- Imban</p><h2>Defense</h2><p>AC 20, touch 8, flat-footed 20 (-1 size, +12 natural, -1 Dex)</p><p>hp 104 [143] (11d8+55)</p><p>Fort +12, Ref +2, Will +5</p><p>Immune plant traits</p><p>Weakness fire</p><h2>Offense</h2><p>Speed 20 ft.</p><p>Melee slam +15 (2d6+10 plus grab and poison)</p><p>Space 10 ft.; Reach 10 ft.</p><p>Special Attacks Electrapulse</p><h2>Statistics</h2><p>Str 25, Dex 9, Con 20, Int 6, Wis 15, Cha 6</p><p>Base Atk +8; CMB +16 (+20 grapple); CMD 25</p><p>Feats Ability Focus (Electrapulse), Blind-Fight, Improved Natural Attack (Slam), Power Attack, Skill Focus (Perception), Weapon Focus (Slam)</p><p>Skills Perception +21</p><p>SQ Treespeech</p><h2>Ecology</h2><p>Environment forests</p><p>Organization small group (1-3)</p><p>Treasure incidental</p>"
      }
